+ * toRoman(4) is "IV", toRoman(1994) is "MCMXCIV", toRoman(3999) is "MMMCMXCIX". The result is
+ * upper case, and each number has exactly one spelling (never "IIII" or "VIIII").
+ * - Roman numerals have no zero or negative numbers, and no standard symbol for 4000 and above, so
+ *   anything outside 1 to 3999 is rejected rather than approximated.
+ * - A whole number written as a float is fine (4.0), but a fraction is not.
+ * @param {number} n integer from 1 to 3999
